    "highlights": "Emphasis and strong states are handled via variable font axes, applying `\"slnt\" -6` for italics and exact `\"wght\"` values (e.g., 550, 600) for bolding text dynamically, avoiding traditional discrete font weights.",
    "insights": [
      "The typography system heavily leverages variable fonts (`font-variation-settings`), fine-tuning width (`wdth`), weight (`wght`), and slant (`slnt`) across breakpoints and semantic tags.",
      "Extensive use of CSS variables (e.g., `--fig-typography-size-title1`) creates a highly flexible, token-driven hierarchy capable of responding to varying viewport sizes seamlessly.",
      "Monospace fonts (`figmaMono`) are strategically used not just for code, but for structural labels, badges, and tertiary headings to introduce technical sophistication into the visual rhythm."
